   "CBB6/7/12/13/14/20 (monovalent, twice in each name)": "(4-(...amino)-2-methylphenyl) attached to the central methine, AND ...-3-methylphenyl)(ethyl)amino cited on the nitrogen"
  },
  "resolution": "The two divalent forms contradict each other under any one locant convention. The monovalent prefixes do not: in a monovalent prefix position 1 IS the attachment, so both of them put the methyl ORTHO to the central methine and META to the nitrogen. The synthesis agrees -- both series come from I2, 3-((ethyl(m-tolyl)amino)methyl)benzenesulfonic acid, whose N-alkyl-m-toluidine is attacked para to the nitrogen (C4), ortho to the C3 methyl.",
  "emitted": "methyl ortho to the central methine in BOTH series",
  "NOT_CHECKABLE_BY_MASS": "every candidate is an isomer; see 08_contradictions.csv row 1"
 },
